{"agent":"buglane7","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new `called_from` exception suppresses the warning/evidence whenever the command's start path resolves to the lease's recorded worktree, even if the caller explicitly identified itself as a different agent. For example, if item `TASK` is leased to `alice` with `lease.worktree=/repo/.lanes/task`, and a user runs `ddflow review TASK --agent bob` from `/repo/.lanes/task`, `ID.resolve` yields `bob`, `_in_its_own_tree` returns True, and `_name_the_item` returns `extra` before emitting the WARNING and before adding the `reviewed_for_holder` evidence. That is wrong because `--agent bob` (or `DDFLOW_AGENT=bob`) is an explicit declaration that the caller is not the lease holder; the bug's fix should avoid the false warning only for the default/derived identity case, not silence the safety warning and audit evidence for an explicitly chosen non-holder identity.","digest":"22e3b4fb890efbde","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/api/review/gate.py:_name_the_item","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/review/gate.py:_name_the_item"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The test asserts that `_name_the_item(repo, cfg, st, \"T1\", \"rubber_duck\", \"bob\", ..., called_from=tree)` produces no warning and no event, where `tree` is T1’s claimed worktree and the lease holder is `alice`. That means the guard is suppressed solely because the call is made from the item’s worktree, even though the identity passed to the review is explicitly `\"bob\"`. If the command surface passes an explicit non-holder identity into `_name_the_item` (e.g. `ddflow review T1 --agent bob` or `DDFLOW_AGENT=bob`), bob can silence the “leased to alice” warning simply by running inside alice’s claimed worktree while still acting as bob. The stated bug is about the *default* identity being wrong in a worktree, not about allowing an explicit wrong identity to bypass the lease guard; this test encodes behavior that defeats the one-identity-per-lease protection.","digest":"aa39be3f93c73bc0","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_review_item_guard.py:test_review_from_the_items_own_tree_under_another_identity_does_not_warn","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_review_item_guard.py:test_review_from_the_items_own_tree_under_another_identity_does_not_warn"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":6595,"diff_sha":"90fac8b146cc5ca4b820e369e15b1467949316b9af02188c6d91942a921fc2e8","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B090201fcef","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":205.3,"family":"alibaba","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"0a33dc3bf3a3fd3f","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B090201fcef.rubber_duck.[REDACTED:name].20261113T061115Z-1b4ecad6.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"88bb05e43bbd71871af8d9ed234096e5b59d38ec","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/review/gate.py":"100644 d717a74d8f6c3175fc9378a13436f2307430eb0e","ddflow/api/review/run.py":"100644 5fab9863d5733a56295fef70637682fa915076fe","ddflow/surfaces/commands/review.py":"100644 c9c255f921a20863d2cc6db402b6ea03aacdb85e","tests/test_review_item_guard.py":"100644 437c8849acd72615a901aa14e51de0cbd8cc694d"},"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","reviewer_families":["alibaba"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/review/gate.py:_name_the_item","tests/test_review_item_guard.py:test_review_from_the_items_own_tree_under_another_identity_does_not_warn"],"tree_sha":"88bb05e43bbd+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e37feedcd093a0637d675729c","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":190933,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B090201fce